# anthropic_vault_credential (Resource)

Creates and manages a vault credential for Anthropic Managed Agents (beta). A credential stores authentication material (bearer tokens, OAuth tokens, or environment variable secrets) that agents can use when calling MCP servers.

> **API**: `POST/GET/PATCH/DELETE /v1/vaults/{vault_id}/credentials[/{id}]` (Managed Agents API).
> **Auth**: Standard API key (`api_key` / `ANTHROPIC_API_KEY`).
> **Beta header**: `anthropic-beta: managed-agents-2026-04-01`.
> **Cost**: Free for management, billable at runtime when the credential is used during an agent session.

## Security Note

**Credential material (`token` / `access_token` / `refresh_token` / `client_secret` / `secret_value`) is a write-only argument, never persisted to Terraform state.** Use `token_wo_version` to rotate secrets: increment the value in your configuration and run `terraform apply`. Anthropic stores and refreshes the credential server-side; the secret is never logged.

## Limits

- Maximum 20 credentials per vault.
- `networking.allowed_hosts` accepts bare hostnames (`api.example.com`), IPv4 addresses (`192.0.2.1`), or `*.`-prefixed wildcards (`*.example.com`). Maximum 16 entries. URLs, ports, paths, and IPv6 addresses are not accepted.

